# On-demand, single-shot hybrid (YOLO crop + image-enhancement cascade +
# classical ArUco + solvePnP) marker detection — added 2026-08-04 for
# calibration_broadcaster_node's per-waypoint hybrid mode
# (hybrid_per_waypoint_enabled), so exactly one detection happens per
# waypoint instead of yolo_marker_bridge_node.py running its full pipeline
# continuously at camera framerate. Served by yolo_marker_bridge_node.py:
# on request, captures the next incoming camera frame and runs it through
# the SAME estimate_marker_pose_cascade() path already used for continuous
# mode (no duplicated cascade logic), returning the result synchronously
# instead of only publishing it to marker_pose.
#
# Empty request — mirrors GetPolygonWaypoints.srv's own empty-request shape
# (this is also a read-only "give me one result" call, not an action that
# changes state elsewhere).
---
bool success
string message
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped marker_pose

# The specific cascade variant that succeeded (e.g. "gamma_0.7",
# "upscale_4x+clahe") — see YOLO-pipeline/config/cascade_real.yaml's own
# variant list. Empty string if success is false. Used by
# calibration_broadcaster_node to label each tile in its combined-grid
# debug image (see that node's own doc comment on hybrid_per_waypoint_enabled).
string cascade_variant_used

# The actual crop image that succeeded detection (JPEG, base64-encoded —
# same encoding inference_server.py's /debug_sweep endpoint already uses
# via _encode_image_b64, reused here rather than inventing a second image
# transport). Empty string if success is false. This is the "how clean are
# the corners" inspection image the calibration_broadcaster_node
# accumulates across a run into one labeled grid, per user's explicit
# request (2026-08-04) for visual confirmation + a presentation artifact —
# not consumed by any other node.
string cascade_image_b64

# Set ONLY when success is false (empty otherwise) — distinguishes WHY the
# marker wasn't found (2026-08-04), mirroring
# estimate_marker_pose_cascade's own two failure_reason values:
#   - "no_yolo_bbox": YOLO itself never found a candidate aruco_marker
#     bounding box in this frame at all — the enhancement cascade never
#     even ran.
#   - "no_classical_match": YOLO DID find a bbox, but classical cv::aruco
#     detection failed on every enhancement variant tried within it.
# Added after a live debugging session where this distinction was only
# ever visible in inference_server.py's own stdout print() logs, which
# weren't reliably captured in the same log file as everything else —
# putting it in the response means calibration_broadcaster_node's own,
# reliably-captured ROS log can report it directly.
string failure_reason
